# RockServer Device Control

- For device-control work, start from `docs/roadmap/device-control-tasks.md`;
  treat `api/openapi.yaml` as the protocol contract and
  `docs/roadmap/device-control-rockcast-esp32.md` as architecture context.
- Reuse existing account pairing, `devices.id`, device secret and native session.
  Derive device-control identity server-side; never create a second device,
  pairing, secret or native-session flow.
- Keep `capabilities`, runtime `state` and `commands` distinct. Roles and
  capabilities describe availability, not authorization. Enforce user ownership
  and explicit scopes; Home Assistant credentials stay separate.
- Do not implement later DC milestones incidentally. Keep WebSocket transport,
  state, commands and public directory APIs within their assigned tasks.
- Default workflow is the saved `master` checkout: no worktree, branch, commit
  or staging unless the user explicitly asks. Preserve unrelated changes.
- Before completion run relevant `cargo fmt --check`, clippy, tests, OpenAPI
  checks and `git diff --check`; report any skipped verification. Update roadmap,
  status and task logs only for acceptance criteria actually completed.
